-- The collection element is used only through explicit casts, so no cast target
-- constrains its origin. It keeps the language default I32, which the final I32
-- cast exposes as an invalid same-type cast (invalid_cast.same_source_and_target).
-- If a cast target wrongly constrained the element, the earlier casts would make
-- the final cast a valid conversion and this diagnostic would vanish.
values = {1, 2}
wide U64 = cast values.get(0) catch:
    then 0
;
signed I64 = cast values.get(0) catch:
    then 0
;
same_default I32 = cast values.get(0) catch:
    then 0
;

[:unreachable]
